// H10.3 (H19): `unsafe` is the deliberate escape hatch and is unchanged.
// The self-host runtime binds local out-parameters inside `unsafe`
// (mir/interpreter.ivy: `lenptr.p = &dec_len;`), so aliasing inside it cannot
// be rejected.  This fixture pins the accepted exception: two mutable
// references and a write while borrowed, all inside `unsafe`, are accepted.
// See H10_NOTES.md H10.3 for the rationale.
void unsafe_escape() {
    int32 x = 1;
    unsafe {
        int32& a = x;
        int32& b = x;
        x = 3;
    }
}